@startuml
title Inside one MPF branch node - proving child 5 costs 4 sibling hashes
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 26
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
  FontColor #16324F
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5

rectangle "**Branch node hash**\nh( nibbles(prefix) || M )" as BH #4A78B5
rectangle "**M** = h( a2 || n8 )\nMerkle root over the 16 slots" as M
rectangle "n8 = subtree over slots 8..15" as N8 #FDEEEE
rectangle "a2 = h( n4 || a1 )" as A2
rectangle "n4 = subtree over slots 0..3" as N4 #FDEEEE
rectangle "a1 = h( a0 || n2 )" as A1
rectangle "n2 = subtree over slots 6..7" as N2 #FDEEEE
rectangle "a0 = h( n1 || root )" as A0
rectangle "n1 = slot 4" as N1 #FDEEEE
rectangle "**root** = sub-trie under slot 5\nrebuilt from the remaining proof steps" as R #EAF6F0

BH --> M
M --> A2
M --> N8
A2 --> N4
A2 --> A1
A1 --> A0
A1 --> N2
A0 --> N1
A0 --> R

note right of N8
  The four pink nodes are the whole
  ""neighbors"" field of one ""Branch"" step:
  4 x 32 = 128 bytes.
  An Ethereum MPT proof would carry
  the 15 remaining child hashes instead.
end note
@enduml
